{
 "id": "u05",
 "n": 5,
 "level": "A1",
 "title": "Questions and negation",
 "summary": "Asking questions and saying no.",
 "explain": [
  {
   "h": "Saying no"
  },
  {
   "p": "Put **no** right before the verb: *Trabajo hoy → **No** trabajo hoy.* With object pronouns, *no* goes before them: *No lo sé.*"
  },
  {
   "p": "Spanish uses **double negatives**. With *nunca, nada, nadie, tampoco* after the verb, keep *no* before it:"
  },
  {
   "ex": [
    "No tengo nada.",
    "I don't have anything."
   ]
  },
  {
   "ex": [
    "No viene nadie.",
    "Nobody is coming."
   ]
  },
  {
   "ex": [
    "No bebo nunca café. / Nunca bebo café.",
    "I never drink coffee."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tip": "If *nunca* or *nadie* comes **before** the verb, drop *no*: *Nunca llega tarde.*"
  },
  {
   "h": "Yes/no questions"
  },
  {
   "p": "Same words as a statement, with question marks at both ends and rising intonation: *¿Tienes coche?* The subject can also move after the verb: *¿Viene el cliente mañana?*"
  },
  {
   "h": "Question words (always with an accent)"
  },
  {
   "table": [
    [
     "¿qué?",
     "what?"
    ],
    [
     "¿quién? / ¿quiénes?",
     "who?"
    ],
    [
     "¿dónde?",
     "where?"
    ],
    [
     "¿adónde?",
     "where to?"
    ],
    [
     "¿cuándo?",
     "when?"
    ],
    [
     "¿cómo?",
     "how?"
    ],
    [
     "¿por qué?",
     "why?"
    ],
    [
     "¿cuánto? / ¿cuánta? / ¿cuántos? / ¿cuántas?",
     "how much? / how many?"
    ],
    [
     "¿cuál? / ¿cuáles?",
     "which (one)?"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "p": "The question word comes first and the verb right after it: *¿Dónde **vives**?* *¿Cuándo **empieza** la obra?*"
  },
  {
   "tip": "*¿Por qué?* (why?) is two words with an accent. *Porque* (because) is one word without."
  }
 ],
